{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c459","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b326-34a5-74f1-8680-2e2c2ca4449b"},"sequence":135,"recorded_at":1780531400000265,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"37553fb7-ae2e-4004-ba6a-caef8cb79aa4","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"37553fb7-ae2e-4004-ba6a-caef8cb79aa4","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"37553fb7-ae2e-4004-ba6a-caef8cb79aa4"},"call_id":"call_01a0b326d8457000a5c6864a6dfeb20e","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2g5be6/TASK-260830-2g5be6_review-verdict-rev3.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2g5be6 — Review verdict, Change Request revision 3\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260918-4b4c38 (claude-opus-5 max, reviewer/reviewer).\n4|Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-2g5be6-3` revision 3, base\n5|`2f844bb49702a860c1199a6a2a0ca6a5cc878197` (the predecessor's checkpoint on the\n6|Story branch), candidate tree `9114b46637f08df16d92727e869bfc846a029069` (22\n7|paths; patch sha256 `6ce030b3b0f6be1329e194968760e6cbc774ae6f137a68199fbb9d03b2cf7c1e`,\n8|verified byte-equal to `git diff 2f844bb 9114b466`). The live Story worktree's\n9|temp-index tree OID (`git add -A` into a scratch index copy) equalled\n10|`9114b466…` before this review and `git status` stayed ` M LOGBOOK.md`,\n11|` M README.md`, `?? internal/clonesnap/` throughout; the worktree, index, branch\n12|and HEAD were never touched. `origin/main` is still `c3aae73` (fetched; no\n13|refresh was due). Authority: `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` §13.14.1 (lines\n14|10331–10546), §10.2 (4851–4903), §7.8 (3738–3924, `ResourceLimits` /\n15|`CapturePlanItem` / capture-plan and capture bodies), re-extracted and\n16|diffed member-for-member against the candidate. (As in rev1 and rev2, the\n17|reviewer brief's \"Section 4.C / terminalbackend\" paragraph is a copy from\n18|another leaf; this review covers the capture scope the task and producer\n19|brief define.)\n20|\n21|## Verdict: ACCEPTED → `accept_cr(TASK-260830-2g5be6, revision=3)`\n22|\n23|No P1, no P2. Both revision-2 P2 rows are closed and MEASURED closed on this\n24|tree: every rev2 survivor re-planted here is KILLED 2/2 by the whole committed\n25|suite (section 0), and the ratio the producer publishes — 17 of 17 AC rows\n26|driven and measured at the member level — is backed by my own battery under\n27|the definition the rev2 verdict used (every member a row NAMES is reached by\n28|a committed test through the named production entry, and a narrowing of that\n29|member reddens it). Production is correct on every probe I drove (25 new\n30|probe lines on the pristine tree, section \"What is clean\"): no admit-hole, no\n31|containment escape, no leak, no fork of a landed gate that changes behaviour.\n32|\n33|What remains is seven P3 evidence gaps and three informational items\n34|(section \"Findings\"): sub-members, axes and sibling refusal arms that no\n35|committed row reaches, each proven by a plant that SURVIVED the whole suite\n36|2/2 with its admitted behaviour executed under the plant. None of them is a\n37|member an AC row names, none changes production, and each is one test plus\n38|one harness row. By the precedent this Story set (the predecessor's rev6 was\n39|accepted with three P3 measurement gaps recorded for the sibling leaves) they\n40|are recorded here as inherited advisories for the Story's FINAL leaf\n41|TASK-260830-32ypr2 or a follow-up on `internal/clonesnap`, not as grounds for\n42|a fourth revision. The orchestrator routes them; this verdict names each with\n43|its exact test shape.\n44|\n45|Method: isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree (`git archive\n46|9114b466…` → `.temp/TASK-260830-2g5be6/review-rev3/{pristine,candidate}` in\n47|the Story worktree's `.temp`, with the tracked `.task-board/.resources` and\n48|`.task-board/.activity` artifacts dropped from both copies to keep scratch\n49|small — the `specpin` board survey needs only `.task-board/**/STORY-*/README.md`,\n50|which stayed); `diff -rq` clean against `pristine` before use and after every\n51|battery, probe and hygiene run. Every probe and plant drove a production entry\n52|(`Capture`, `CaptureAndProject`, `AdmitForTarget`, `BuildAdmissionReceipt`,\n53|`CheckpointWorkspace`); `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1` for every harness, zero\n54|`__pycache__`/`.pyc` in any copy or in the candidate tree. Raw evidence:\n55|`TASK-260830-2g5be6_review-evidence-rev3.tar.gz` (`logs/`, one raw `go test`\n56|log per plant per run under `logs/mutants/run{1,2}/` (31 each) and\n57|`logs/mutants-producer/run{1,2}/` (44 each), `logs/under-mutant/` executions\n58|of each survivor, `reviewer_mutants_rev3.py`, `run_under_mutant.py`, the two\n59|probe files as `.txt`, `logs/probes-pristine.log` (25 `PROBE` lines),\n60|`logs/crash-rev3-run{1,2}.log`, `logs/refusal-site-census.txt`,\n61|`logs/hygiene.log`, `MANIFEST.sha256`).\n62|\n63|## 0. Rework verification (rev2 findings against the NEW tree)\n64|\n65|| rev2 finding | rev3 change | re-plant (whole suite, 2 runs) | Verdict |\n66||---|---|---|---|\n67|| P2-α row 8 (sealed unstable pre/post digests unpinned) | `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable` asserts decoded `CaptureBoundary.Pre/PostCaptureDigest == result.Pre/PostDigest` and `SourceGeneration == request.Generation` (`race_test.go:161-175`) | `R2-unstable-seals-pre-as-post` **KILLED 2/2** (killer `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable`, `race_test.go:168: sealed post_capture_digest = sha256:7113…, measured post = \"sha256:d7e2…\"`) | closed (see P3-a for the labelling sub-member) |\n68|| P2-α row 10 (\"before any seal\" unpinned at `CaptureAndProject`) | `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt` scans the CAPTURE store (`storeSink`, the `request.Store` sink — verified it is the capture store, not the target) for any decodable raw or capture manifest (`race_test.go:256-263`) | `R2-project-seal-before-gate` **KILLED 2/2** (killer `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt`, `race_test.go:258: mutated capture sealed a raw manifest before the race gate`) | closed |\n69|| P3-a unplanned SPECIAL member | `TestCaptureRefusesUnplannedSpecialMember` (unplanned symlink `stray-link` → outside secret; refusal names it, no outside byte, zero blobs) | `R2-unplanned-special-admitted` **KILLED 2/2** | closed |\n70|| P3-b symlinked STORE root | `TestCaptureRefusesSymlinkedStoreRoot` (refusal names `link-root` + `symlink`, zero blobs) | `R2-store-root-follows-symlink` (the rev2 widening, `os.Open` at the root) **KILLED 2/2** | closed |\n71|| P3-c excluded member size change | `TestCaptureRaceExcludedSizeChange` (shipped the row, not the reword) | `R2-excluded-size-ignored` **KILLED 2/2** | closed |\n72|| P3-d branch bound attribution | TRACEABILITY 1.6 row names the landed `DecodeWorkspaceBinding` as the measured gate, local check = defence in depth, with a first-hand survival probe (`attribution/branch-bound-landed-decoder.log`, exit 0) | `R2-branch-1025` **SURVIVED 2/2** as attributed (the landed decoder is the backstop). Note: on the pristine tree the LOCAL check fires first (`workspace.go:179` executed, the decoder refusal at `workspace.go:100` is never reached by the suite); the decoder \"refuses first\" only under the narrowing — wording, not substance | closed |\n73|| P3-e four pinned gates with no row | `N-plan-grammar-dotdot`, `N-required-blocked-ancestor`, `N-fingerprints-129`, `N-first-chunk-oversize` shipped | my `R2-plan-grammar-admits-dotdot`, `R2-required-blockedAncestor-dropped`, `R2-fingerprints-129`, `R2-first-chunk-oversize` all **KILLED 2/2** | closed |\n74|| Ratio restated | results/matrix/LOGBOOK publish 17 of 17 with the killer of every row named, and the finding-by-finding table | measured, see \"Measured ratio\" | closed |\n75|\n76|The four new harness rows measure what their names claim: `N-unstable-seals-pre-as-post`\n77|is a narrowing (the `state.pre` digest sealed for `post_capture_digest`,