r-post-measure | seam control | KILLED 2/2 | 13 tests |\n345|| R3-archive-swaps-pre-post | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-a) |\n346|| R3-archive-policy-always-unstable | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-b) |\n347|| R3-post-measure-only-with-hook | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-e, bound) |\n348|| R3-post-enumerate-failure-as-quiet | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-c) |\n349|| R3-enumerate-unreadable-as-empty | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-d) |\n350|| R3-receipt-profile-unchecked | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-f) |\n351|| R3-drop-early-containment-pass | arm-delete (labelled) | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-g ii) |\n352|| R3-empty-cwd-as-root | narrowing | **SURVIVED 2/2** | — (P3-g i) |\n353|| R3-early-pass-opens-excluded-special | arm-delete (over-strict) | SURVIVED 2/2 | — (informational) |\n354|| R3-nil-target-sink-unchecked | arm-delete | SURVIVED 2/2 | — (informational) |\n355|| R3-archive-not-core | narrowing (landed rule reached from this entry) | KILLED 2/2 | TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable, TestProjectRefusesUnstable, TestProjectRefusesUnstableDirect |\n356|| C-stable-seals-pre-as-post | equivalence control | SURVIVED 2/2 (expected) | — |\n357|| C-rev3-comment | harmless control | SURVIVED 2/2 (expected) | — |\n358|\n359|18 KILLED, 13 SURVIVED (3 expected, 10 findings-bearing), 0 ERROR; every\n360|row's raw log carries `# exit=` and the plant text; the candidate copy was\n361|`diff -rq`-clean against pristine after both runs.\n362|\n363|## Measured ratio\n364|\n365|**17 of 17 AC rows driven through the named production entry by a named\n366|committed test, and 17 of 17 measured at the member level** — every member a\n367|row names is reached and a narrowing of it reddens the row's killer (rows 8\n368|and 10, the rev2 gaps, are now KILLED by `TestCaptureArchiveSealsUnstable`\n369|and `TestCaptureRaceEmitsNoReceipt`). Beyond the named members, 8 plants on\n370|sub-members, axes and sibling refusal arms survive (P3-a..g above); rows 8\n371|(labelling; archive-policy × quiet axis), 9/10 (enumeration-failure arm;\n372|seam-only bound), 12 (empty cwd) and 17 (standalone receipt entry) carry\n373|them. Refusal-arm census: 25 of 60 refusal sites executed by the committed\n374|suite, 9 reachable arms without a row (all P3 or informational above).\n375|\n376|## Advisories carried forward (for the orchestrator to route — Story FINAL leaf TASK-260830-32ypr2 or a follow-up on `internal/clonesnap`)\n377|\n378|1. P3-a: independent oracle for the archive digests (`pre_capture_digest ==\n379|   quiet capture digest`), harness row `R3-archive-swaps-pre-post`.\n380|2. P3-b: one quiet-store row under `RaceArchive` + `OperatorExplicit`\n381|   (`BoundaryKind == \"stable\"`, admits), harness row\n382|   `R3-archive-policy-always-unstable`.\n383|3. P3-c/d: two chmod-000 rows (store subdirectory unreadable at post; planned\n384|   optional member in an unlistable directory at walk), skip for euid 0,\n385|   harness rows `R3-post-enumerate-failure-as-quiet` /\n386|   `R3-enumerate-unreadable-as-empty`; or restate the `walk.go` \"never an\n387|   absence\" comment as a bound.\n388|4. P3-e: state the AfterWalk-seam bound in TRACEABILITY and the results.\n389|5. P3-f: one direct `BuildAdmissionReceipt(…, \"ultra\")` refusal row, harness\n390|   row `R3-receipt-profile-unchecked`; or state the standalone-entry bound\n391|   beside P3-η.\n392|6. P3-g: empty-cwd refusal row; early-pass \"nothing installed\" row (planned\n393|   special sorted after an included member, zero blobs) or reword.\n394|7. Inherited from rev2/predecessor and still open by design: P3-ζ\n395|   (lone-surrogate at `validText`), P3-η remainder (`EncodeNativeIdentity`\n396|   standalone), P3-ζ′ (fidelity vocabulary spelled twice — now also the\n397|   four-class exclusion table), all deferred to the final leaf as the\n398|   producer states.\n399|\n400|Checklist state left by this review: reviewer rows \"Implementation matches\n401|AC\", \"Solution fits project architecture\", \"Tests green\" and \"Gate, refusal,\n402|validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read\" are\n403|checked (each measured true: every named gate carries a killed narrowing;\n404|positive-path-only evidence remains only on the P3 sub-members recorded\n405|above); \"If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and\n406|status routed\" is checked (not applicable on acceptance; the verdict\n407|evidence is attached). Status routed by `accept_cr` to `integrating`.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
